# Net Sales Trend Analysis
**Period: Nov 2024 – Oct 2025**

## Key Observations

- **Strong Jan 2025 spike:** Net Sales reached RM 9.69M (+56% vs Nov baseline), driven by Invoice Sales jump to RM 8.16M and Cash Sales surge to RM 1.60M. Likely seasonal (Chinese New Year/festive demand).

- **Stabilization post-spike:** Months Feb–Oct averaged RM 7.27M. No sustained 3+ month growth or decline detected; trend is **neutral/stable** since February.

- **Cash Sales erosion:** Dropped from RM 1.60M (Jan) to RM 0.30M (Oct) — a 81% decline. Indicates shift back to invoice-based sales after January peak.

- **Credit Notes volatility:** Feb 2025 spiked to RM 135.7K (highest), then normalized. Oct 2025 reached RM 126.3K (second highest). No clear seasonal pattern.

| Period | Min Net Sales | Max Net Sales | Variance |
|--------|---------------|---------------|----------|
| Nov–Dec 2024 | RM 6.11M | RM 6.22M | Flat |
| Jan–Oct 2025 | RM 6.05M | RM 9.69M | Jan spike outlier |

## Flag
Jan 2025 anomaly warrants investigation—confirm if promotional/holiday-driven or one-time customer event.

